Summary:
The macOS VSOCK implementation works by creating a complete emulation layer that translates VSOCK operations into Unix domain socket operations while maintaining the same.
The SharedFD abstraction handles platform differences at the file descriptor level, the vhost_user_vsock device provides VirtIO compatibility, and the overall system uses Hypervisor.framework instead of KVM for virtualization.

This "emulated VSOCK" approach  provides VSOCK functionality on macOS.

Main changes:
Eventfd Emulation Using Pipes
Eventfd Read/Write Emulation
Inotify Replacement with Kqueue

VSOCK Communication Implementation for macOS uses Unix Domain Socket Emulation

ADB Command → socket_vsock_proxy → Unix Socket → vhost_user_vsock →
VirtIO Protocol → Guest VirtIO Driver →
AF_VSOCK → adbd

